1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,033
Characters, actions, places, occupations, and events in this series are fictional and created for entertainment purposes only.

2
00:00:07,033 --> 00:00:10,716
They are not intended to urge or promote any behavior in the series.

3
00:00:10,716 --> 00:00:13,161
Viewer discretion is advised

4
00:01:51,819 --> 00:01:55,664
(A few years ago, my father passed away
from a chronic illness.)

5
00:01:55,664 --> 00:01:57,344
WITH LOVE AND DEEPEST SYMPATHY ALONEWW CO., LTD.
WITH LOVE AND DEEPEST SYMPATHY
FROM SAHARACH THUANMUANG

6
00:01:57,344 --> 00:01:58,838
(He was 60 years old.)

7
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:02,340
MR. JIRA JAROENWONG
BORN FEBRUARY 3, 1960, DIED APRIL 18, 2020
(I think he’s gone too soon.)

8
00:02:03,160 --> 00:02:05,255
(Why couldn’t he live to 70 or 80?)

9
00:02:19,550 --> 00:02:20,909
(But who would have thought…)

10
00:02:22,161 --> 00:02:24,853
(That my life would only be half as long as his.)

11
00:02:31,363 --> 00:02:32,614
(My dad’s gone.)

12
00:02:33,889 --> 00:02:36,539
(My sister got married and moved overseas
with her husband.)

13
00:02:37,859 --> 00:02:39,096
(My mom went along with them.)

14
00:02:47,481 --> 00:02:48,336
(Friends?)

15
00:02:49,588 --> 00:02:50,328
(I have none.)

16
00:02:52,149 --> 00:02:53,034
(Lover?)

17
00:02:54,377 --> 00:02:55,601
(I don’t have that, either.)

18
00:03:06,869 --> 00:03:09,530
(Is that… the class president?)

19
00:03:10,827 --> 00:03:12,861
(If the person lying here were him…)

20
00:03:14,864 --> 00:03:17,161
(He’d have many things to think about
before he died.)

21
00:03:18,550 --> 00:03:20,260
(In that final moment,)

22
00:03:22,377 --> 00:03:25,536
(I finally realized what I regretted most
about my 30 years of life.)

23
00:03:28,814 --> 00:03:31,240
(I didn’t regret that no one remembered me.)

24
00:03:35,065 --> 00:03:38,162
(What I regretted was living my life without remembering anyone.)

25
00:03:57,717 --> 00:03:59,918
(Is this heaven or hell?)

26
00:04:01,534 --> 00:04:02,779
(Why does it feel like…)

27
00:04:04,577 --> 00:04:06,110
(I’m taking a nap at my old house?)

28
00:04:08,455 --> 00:04:09,220
Wait!

29
00:04:10,449 --> 00:04:11,469
My old house?

30
00:04:21,487 --> 00:04:22,776
Get up already.

31
00:04:23,095 --> 00:04:25,278
Stop making that confused face and mumbling.

32
00:04:31,697 --> 00:04:32,788
Where am I?

33
00:04:33,972 --> 00:04:36,190
You think you’re the main character in a novel?

34
00:04:36,668 --> 00:04:38,680
Scoot over.

35
00:04:42,800 --> 00:04:44,641
Why are you dressed like this?

36
00:04:45,460 --> 00:04:46,148
Ji!

37
00:04:47,241 --> 00:04:48,428
Watch your mouth.

38
00:04:48,769 --> 00:04:50,799
I carried you all the way home.

39
00:04:51,004 --> 00:04:52,692
You didn’t even say thank you.

40
00:04:53,307 --> 00:04:54,050
Carried?

41
00:04:54,824 --> 00:04:56,274
Why did you have to carry me?

42
00:04:57,480 --> 00:05:00,926
Wasn’t it you who wanted to go out
to join the water fight

43
00:05:01,017 --> 00:05:03,263
then got heatstroke and passed out in the alley?

44
00:05:03,809 --> 00:05:05,738
You freaked those people out.

45
00:05:24,532 --> 00:05:26,575
Oh, I remember now.

46
00:05:28,077 --> 00:05:29,026
Remember what?

47
00:05:30,096 --> 00:05:33,715
(But wasn’t that... Songkran from years ago?)

48
00:05:35,491 --> 00:05:36,853
(Then why…)

49
00:05:38,401 --> 00:05:39,443
Are you alright?

50
00:05:40,126 --> 00:05:45,709
Did you hit your head and lose your memory?

51
00:05:48,691 --> 00:05:51,166
Damn it. What the hell is going on?

52
00:05:52,077 --> 00:05:54,219
Am I dreaming?

53
00:05:56,768 --> 00:05:57,740
Ouch!

54
00:05:58,537 --> 00:06:00,970
Did your dad tell you to pinch my leg?!

55
00:06:01,881 --> 00:06:04,119
Wait, we have the same dad.

56
00:06:04,825 --> 00:06:05,559
Oww.

57
00:06:08,905 --> 00:06:11,726
(That means… this is really not a dream?)

58
00:06:14,617 --> 00:06:15,393
Mhee!

59
00:06:18,716 --> 00:06:20,075
I miss you so much.

60
00:06:21,486 --> 00:06:22,752
I really miss you.

61
00:06:22,889 --> 00:06:24,978
What are you guys yelling about?

62
00:06:27,140 --> 00:06:27,927
Mom!

63
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:32,577
Mom, this brat… He pinched me.

64
00:06:33,374 --> 00:06:35,750
How many times have I told you
not to call him that?

65
00:06:35,750 --> 00:06:37,174
You, too, Ji.

66
00:06:37,174 --> 00:06:38,841
What did you do to your sister?

67
00:06:39,797 --> 00:06:41,434
I’m bruised, see?

68
00:06:43,369 --> 00:06:45,165
2010.

69
00:06:45,757 --> 00:06:46,971
That means…

70
00:06:51,500 --> 00:06:53,472
Mom called and told me you passed out.

71
00:06:54,337 --> 00:06:58,172
I told you to wait
and go with us in the evening.

72
00:07:07,960 --> 00:07:10,178
MR. JIRAPHAT JAROENWONG
BORN FEBRUARY 3, 1960, DIED APRIL 18, 2020

73
00:07:15,914 --> 00:07:16,915
Dad!

74
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:20,040
Hey, wait, wait, wait.

75
00:07:20,905 --> 00:07:22,720
Why are you hugging me, huh?

76
00:07:26,612 --> 00:07:27,258
Hey.

77
00:07:27,986 --> 00:07:29,684
Are you crying?

78
00:07:30,663 --> 00:07:32,789
Did Jean pick on you?

79
00:07:32,993 --> 00:07:35,201
-I didn’t. This brat…
-Watch it!

80
00:07:35,747 --> 00:07:38,090
Ji pinched me first.

81
00:07:39,670 --> 00:07:40,449
What is it?

82
00:07:41,473 --> 00:07:43,748
Okay, okay, okay.

83
00:08:07,163 --> 00:08:14,258
JIRA, NARUMON, JEAN

84
00:08:26,902 --> 00:08:30,522
AAH! What the hell is this?!

85
00:08:35,666 --> 00:08:36,442
A dream?

86
00:08:37,717 --> 00:08:39,881
If this is just a dream,

87
00:08:40,860 --> 00:08:42,802
I’ll wake up in my bed in my condo.

88
00:08:53,478 --> 00:08:54,699
It’s just a dream.

89
00:08:57,226 --> 00:08:59,800
It’s just a dream. That’s all.

90
00:09:02,349 --> 00:09:03,554
Go to sleep.

91
00:09:40,126 --> 00:09:42,667
(Ji, wake up!)

92
00:09:43,168 --> 00:09:45,355
(You’re gonna sleep in every day
during school break?)

93
00:09:46,106 --> 00:09:47,439
Okay, I’m up.

94
00:09:47,553 --> 00:09:51,524
(Then come down for breakfast.
Mom and Dad are waiting.)

95
00:09:51,524 --> 00:09:53,744
(I’m gonna be late for dorm check-in.)

96
00:09:53,744 --> 00:09:54,576
I heard you.

97
00:10:00,131 --> 00:10:04,059
Did I... really travel back in time?

98
00:10:10,274 --> 00:10:11,768
Ahh!

99
00:10:12,314 --> 00:10:14,871
-Ji, get up!
-Fine!

100
00:10:17,307 --> 00:10:19,884
Finish your breakfast. I’m gonna be late.

101
00:10:19,884 --> 00:10:21,629
I’ll drive you there so fast.

102
00:10:23,427 --> 00:10:24,321
Eat a lot.

103
00:10:25,391 --> 00:10:26,724
There’s plenty of food.

104
00:10:27,475 --> 00:10:28,604
You’re not hungry?

105
00:10:28,604 --> 00:10:29,637
Don’t you like the food?

106
00:10:29,637 --> 00:10:30,579
I do.

107
00:10:34,631 --> 00:10:35,508
This is good.

108
00:10:38,149 --> 00:10:40,577
You need to eat plenty of healthy food, Dad.

109
00:10:42,125 --> 00:10:44,168
You should also cut back on alcohol and beer.

110
00:10:45,534 --> 00:10:47,775
Why are you so worried about me, hmm?

111
00:10:48,116 --> 00:10:49,507
Eat lots of protein.

112
00:10:50,895 --> 00:10:52,642
Such a suck-up.

113
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:55,120
Eat a lot.

114
00:10:55,439 --> 00:10:56,191
Yes, Mom.

115
00:10:59,492 --> 00:11:00,945
Jean, you didn’t forget anything, did you?

116
00:11:00,945 --> 00:11:02,238
No, Mom.

117
00:11:02,375 --> 00:11:04,846
But if I did, I can come back and get it later.

118
00:11:04,846 --> 00:11:07,472
Call me when you get to the dorm, okay?

119
00:11:07,472 --> 00:11:09,999
Eh? You’re not coming with me?

120
00:11:11,387 --> 00:11:13,563
I have to make desserts for my customers.

121
00:11:13,563 --> 00:11:14,873
I really can’t go.

122
00:11:15,192 --> 00:11:17,065
But it’s three months.

123
00:11:17,065 --> 00:11:17,973
Oh, please.

124
00:11:17,973 --> 00:11:20,615
You’re a senior. Don’t act like a child.

125
00:11:20,615 --> 00:11:21,558
You brat.

126
00:11:21,558 --> 00:11:23,246
“You brat. You brat”

127
00:11:23,246 --> 00:11:26,038
-I told you not to call him that.
-Right.

128
00:11:26,038 --> 00:11:28,330
And you, stop messing with your sister.

129
00:11:28,330 --> 00:11:31,315
When she’s gone, you’re gonna be lonely.

130
00:11:31,975 --> 00:11:32,889
I won’t.

131
00:11:34,346 --> 00:11:36,083
Drive safely, honey.

132
00:11:36,083 --> 00:11:37,639
I know, honey.

133
00:11:38,026 --> 00:11:39,270
Come on, Jean.

134
00:11:40,021 --> 00:11:42,413
-Give me a hug.
-Bye-bye, Mom.

135
00:11:43,232 --> 00:11:44,777
See you, Mom.

136
00:11:44,777 --> 00:11:45,721
Give me a hug.

137
00:11:47,838 --> 00:11:49,144
-Bye-bye.
-Let’s go.

138
00:11:49,531 --> 00:11:50,713
My hair’s messed up.

139
00:11:54,150 --> 00:11:55,131
Bye.

140
00:11:56,747 --> 00:11:58,402
Come help me make the desserts.

141
00:11:58,402 --> 00:11:59,241
Okay, Mom.

142
00:12:10,367 --> 00:12:11,553
I broke it again.

143
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:15,070
Thai desserts take lots of patience to make.

144
00:12:16,003 --> 00:12:17,286
I’m trying to be patient.

145
00:12:19,062 --> 00:12:20,320
Go find something to do.

146
00:12:20,775 --> 00:12:22,162
I can do this myself.

147
00:12:23,551 --> 00:12:24,853
But I want to help you.

148
00:12:25,194 --> 00:12:28,733
But I think I can do it faster by myself.

149
00:12:28,733 --> 00:12:29,594
Mom.

150
00:12:30,800 --> 00:12:33,785
It’s your school break. I want you to relax.

151
00:12:33,785 --> 00:12:35,162
If you don’t know where to go,

152
00:12:35,162 --> 00:12:38,417
grab the money on the TV and go get
some ice-cream.

153
00:12:39,828 --> 00:12:41,650
I’m not a kid. I don’t eat ice-cream.

154
00:12:42,424 --> 00:12:43,352
Hmm?

155
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:48,780
Oh.

156
00:12:56,132 --> 00:13:00,921
NARONGRIT BOXING GYM

157
00:13:14,211 --> 00:13:15,439
I’ve read this already.

158
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:26,400
I’ve read this, too.

159
00:13:33,639 --> 00:13:35,706
Isn’t there something new, Chok?

160
00:13:36,594 --> 00:13:39,333
But the one in your hand’s just arrived today, Ji.

161
00:13:51,160 --> 00:13:53,024
(He’s a generous man.)

162
00:13:53,752 --> 00:13:55,906
Ms. Orn still looks beautiful.

163
00:14:13,626 --> 00:14:15,005
The school is about to start.

164
00:14:15,005 --> 00:14:16,665
Why don’t you go out with your friends?

165
00:14:17,189 --> 00:14:19,945
Don’t you get bored being at home all the time?

166
00:14:21,629 --> 00:14:22,729
I don’t, Mom.

167
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:26,414
I love having you at home

168
00:14:26,414 --> 00:14:29,006
but I want you to go out like other kids sometimes.

169
00:14:30,281 --> 00:14:34,130
In case one day your dad, Jean, and I are gone.

170
00:14:34,836 --> 00:14:37,106
I don’t want you to cry all by yourself.

171
00:14:37,106 --> 00:14:38,176
Do you understand?

172
00:15:10,585 --> 00:15:13,583
(To have other things to think about when I die,)

173
00:15:13,970 --> 00:15:16,295
(this Jiraphat will become a new person.)

174
00:15:26,265 --> 00:15:27,435
This year…

175
00:15:28,869 --> 00:15:30,700
2010.

176
00:15:31,997 --> 00:15:35,918
Until the day I die…

177
00:15:45,731 --> 00:15:47,118
2023.

178
00:15:50,145 --> 00:15:51,440
That means

179
00:15:57,632 --> 00:15:59,337
I have...

180
00:16:00,316 --> 00:16:02,932
13 years left to start over.

181
00:16:16,685 --> 00:16:19,380
I was told you guys were smoking.

182
00:16:19,380 --> 00:16:20,411
-I…
-Go!

183
00:16:20,639 --> 00:16:22,697
Go to the disciplinary office now.

184
00:16:22,697 --> 00:16:23,396
Excuse me.

185
00:16:43,657 --> 00:16:45,442
If you run to school, you can get there
in time, right?

186
00:16:45,832 --> 00:16:48,110
Your school is just around the corner.

187
00:16:51,866 --> 00:16:53,806
I don’t mind if you’re late.

188
00:16:54,231 --> 00:16:56,232
But you got up so early today.

189
00:16:56,232 --> 00:16:58,425
Do you want to arrive late anyway?

190
00:17:00,396 --> 00:17:01,102
Huh, Ji?

191
00:17:02,498 --> 00:17:04,441
See you then, Dad.

192
00:17:04,564 --> 00:17:05,211
Yeah.

193
00:17:06,360 --> 00:17:07,978
(This might seem silly.)

194
00:17:08,328 --> 00:17:10,751
(Will going to school early change anything?)

195
00:17:11,982 --> 00:17:14,041
(But for me who hadn’t made any progress)

196
00:17:14,492 --> 00:17:16,564
(from when my dad passed to the day I died,)

197
00:17:17,631 --> 00:17:20,145
(running forward as fast as I can,)

198
00:17:20,145 --> 00:17:21,274
Run, Ji, run!

199
00:17:22,772 --> 00:17:24,727
(It’s not just about getting to school in time.)

200
00:17:26,909 --> 00:17:31,038
(It’s my very first step to move forward
from my meaningless life.)

201
00:17:47,796 --> 00:17:48,456
Yes!

202
00:17:52,204 --> 00:17:54,676
NAWINA SCHOOL

203
00:17:56,913 --> 00:17:57,607
Yes!

204
00:18:05,023 --> 00:18:10,245
♪ Thailand unites Thai people with flesh and blood. ♪

205
00:19:11,966 --> 00:19:16,952
PHAPPIM, LAWYER, IS NOT WORRIED THAT THE OPPOSING PARTY IS INFLUENTIAL. “UNDUE INFLUENCE CANNOT OVERRIDE THE LAW.”

206
00:19:16,952 --> 00:19:17,915
Jiraphat.

207
00:19:20,328 --> 00:19:21,803
Did you run away from the teachers?

208
00:19:23,958 --> 00:19:26,522
-No, I didn’t…
-What are you doing?

209
00:19:27,671 --> 00:19:30,200
Hey, Ji. You’re not late, today?

210
00:19:30,405 --> 00:19:32,229
It’s the first day of school so I’m here early.

211
00:19:32,328 --> 00:19:35,629
But last semester, you were late since the first day.

212
00:19:35,629 --> 00:19:36,318
Mmm.

213
00:19:36,913 --> 00:19:39,614
Well, this semester is different because…

214
00:19:40,538 --> 00:19:41,384
-Because?
-Because?

215
00:19:44,688 --> 00:19:46,559
Because I’m gonna be a good boy this semester!

216
00:19:54,452 --> 00:19:56,363
Don’t laugh at him.

217
00:19:56,527 --> 00:19:58,410
No, I’m not.

218
00:20:00,161 --> 00:20:01,597
Sorry, sorry.

219
00:20:01,597 --> 00:20:04,901
It’s just you talk like my nephew
who’s in kindergarten.

220
00:20:05,558 --> 00:20:08,541
And you made a funny face.

221
00:20:09,238 --> 00:20:10,770
I couldn’t help but laugh a little.

222
00:20:10,888 --> 00:20:11,998
A little?

223
00:20:13,989 --> 00:20:16,876
But you seemed confident when you said that.

224
00:20:17,040 --> 00:20:19,868
I’ll believe you didn’t come to school late.

225
00:20:21,838 --> 00:20:24,527
Here’s the list of students in Grade 11, Class 7,
Miss Prefect.

226
00:20:24,773 --> 00:20:25,829
Got it.

227
00:20:26,670 --> 00:20:28,538
I’ll go to the restroom now.

228
00:20:30,118 --> 00:20:32,529
Now that you’re here in time,
don’t cut classes again.

229
00:20:36,305 --> 00:20:39,437
Hey, I’m sorry I laughed at you.

230
00:20:39,847 --> 00:20:42,560
And don’t worry. What you said earlier,

231
00:20:42,663 --> 00:20:43,730
I won’t tell anyone.

232
00:20:45,967 --> 00:20:47,137
See you in class.

233
00:20:58,952 --> 00:20:59,638
Look.

234
00:20:59,638 --> 00:21:01,608
Jiraphat, The Good Boy’s here, everyone.

235
00:21:01,608 --> 00:21:02,817
A round of applause.

236
00:21:03,700 --> 00:21:05,790
Woohoo!

237
00:21:06,478 --> 00:21:10,128
MONDAY, MAY 17

238
00:21:14,192 --> 00:21:15,439
Listen up, guys.

239
00:21:16,014 --> 00:21:17,469
I have news

240
00:21:17,715 --> 00:21:19,502
on Jiraphat, The Good Boy.

241
00:21:19,748 --> 00:21:20,427
Huh?

242
00:21:20,714 --> 00:21:23,269
Jiraphat, The Good Boy.

243
00:21:24,336 --> 00:21:25,165
What?

244
00:21:26,328 --> 00:21:27,677
Welcome, The Good Boy.

245
00:21:30,530 --> 00:21:31,524
Hi, Ji!

246
00:21:40,426 --> 00:21:41,243
Hi.

247
00:21:45,553 --> 00:21:46,867
How was your school break?

248
00:21:47,134 --> 00:21:48,656
It was good. You?

249
00:21:50,852 --> 00:21:51,778
I had so much fun.

250
00:21:51,778 --> 00:21:53,947
This year, my dad took me on a Songkran trip.

251
00:21:54,029 --> 00:21:55,762
We went to Silom, Khaosan,

252
00:21:55,762 --> 00:21:56,826
and around our house.

253
00:21:56,826 --> 00:21:59,312
They even put ice in the water they used.

254
00:21:59,312 --> 00:22:02,442
(I had a nice friend who sat next to me in class.)

255
00:22:05,993 --> 00:22:07,424
(But when I died,)

256
00:22:07,609 --> 00:22:09,038
(why didn’t I think of him?)

257
00:22:09,141 --> 00:22:09,919
(Hi, Ji!)

258
00:22:12,217 --> 00:22:12,861
Hi, Ji!

259
00:22:13,148 --> 00:22:13,866
Mmm.

260
00:22:14,872 --> 00:22:16,166
How was your school break?

261
00:22:16,700 --> 00:22:17,438
It was fine.

262
00:22:26,576 --> 00:22:28,595
Hey, Ked. Hey, Pim.

263
00:22:29,272 --> 00:22:29,965
Yeah?

264
00:22:31,073 --> 00:22:33,248
After the mid-term exam, I’m moving to England.

265
00:22:34,459 --> 00:22:36,125
I won’t see you guys anymore.

266
00:22:36,905 --> 00:22:38,347
Why move there so suddenly?

267
00:22:38,675 --> 00:22:41,492
My dad has to move for work quite often.

268
00:22:41,492 --> 00:22:43,072
So we have to move with him.

269
00:22:43,236 --> 00:22:44,343
But I’m used to it now.

270
00:22:44,902 --> 00:22:46,038
You two are going to miss me.

271
00:22:49,096 --> 00:22:50,925
Wanna go together next year?

272
00:22:56,712 --> 00:22:57,483
What?

273
00:22:59,535 --> 00:23:01,052
You want to hang out with me?

274
00:23:03,186 --> 00:23:05,585
I’m gonna cry right now.

275
00:23:08,828 --> 00:23:10,683
Let’s plan our Songkran trip for next year, Ji.

276
00:23:13,269 --> 00:23:15,246
Attention, students.

277
00:23:16,170 --> 00:23:18,456
All Good morning.

278
00:23:18,600 --> 00:23:20,102
Good morning, everyone.

279
00:23:20,102 --> 00:23:22,539
We’ve met before in social studies class.

280
00:23:22,539 --> 00:23:24,798
But today, I’d like to introduce myself again.

281
00:23:24,798 --> 00:23:26,100
I’m Mr. Tinnapob.

282
00:23:26,100 --> 00:23:27,012
You can call me Mr. Tin.

283
00:23:27,238 --> 00:23:29,214
I’ll be your homeroom teacher for Grade 11, Class 7,

284
00:23:29,214 --> 00:23:30,565
this academic year.

285
00:23:30,729 --> 00:23:31,674
Nice to see you all.

286
00:23:50,814 --> 00:23:51,935
Please, I have to get to class.

287
00:23:52,223 --> 00:23:53,377
What’s the problem?!

288
00:24:00,930 --> 00:24:01,457
Why so scared?

289
00:24:01,909 --> 00:24:03,424
-Hey, you.
-Come on, try this.

290
00:24:03,424 --> 00:24:04,407
We’re at school.

291
00:24:09,782 --> 00:24:10,684
None of your business!

292
00:24:16,513 --> 00:24:17,551
Jiraphat.

293
00:24:18,639 --> 00:24:20,043
Jiraphat, The Good Boy, right?

294
00:24:20,328 --> 00:24:21,928
You can’t smoke in school.

295
00:24:21,928 --> 00:24:22,552
Why not?

296
00:24:22,552 --> 00:24:24,888
Jiraphat, The Good Boy is worried about my health?

297
00:24:24,888 --> 00:24:27,229
You can smoke 100 cigarettes a day if you want.

298
00:24:27,229 --> 00:24:28,558
I don’t even care.

299
00:24:28,825 --> 00:24:30,360
But I just want to warn you.

300
00:24:30,360 --> 00:24:32,882
If you keep smoking like this,
you’re gonna die someday.

301
00:24:32,882 --> 00:24:34,461
But not from lung cancer.

302
00:24:34,461 --> 00:24:37,978
-But from smoking where you shouldn’t.
-You jackass!

303
00:24:38,922 --> 00:24:39,976
Kongpob!

304
00:24:39,976 --> 00:24:40,848
Jiraphat!

305
00:24:46,985 --> 00:24:49,574
I was told you guys were smoking.

306
00:24:51,093 --> 00:24:52,306
-I…
-Go!

307
00:24:53,517 --> 00:24:55,321
Go to the disciplinary office now.

308
00:24:58,235 --> 00:24:59,199
Excuse me.

309
00:25:07,410 --> 00:25:08,810
I was in the toilet.

310
00:25:09,528 --> 00:25:11,054
Jiraphat wasn’t smoking.

311
00:25:13,702 --> 00:25:15,014
I think you’re misinformed.

312
00:25:18,400 --> 00:25:19,780
I got it, Atiwitch.

313
00:25:20,211 --> 00:25:21,509
You get to class.

314
00:25:22,535 --> 00:25:26,150
Jiraphat, you go to the disciplinary office.

315
00:25:27,340 --> 00:25:28,382
-But, sir.
-But, sir.

316
00:25:29,326 --> 00:25:30,522
What’s wrong with you guys?

317
00:25:30,974 --> 00:25:34,897
You think I don’t know.
Jiraphat is always late to school.

318
00:25:35,595 --> 00:25:37,418
But when school’s over,

319
00:25:37,418 --> 00:25:40,033
he’s always the first to run out.

320
00:25:40,875 --> 00:25:45,531
Do you think this guy will get himself in trouble
and get detention after school?

321
00:25:45,777 --> 00:25:47,675
You smell like smoke.

322
00:25:47,675 --> 00:25:48,933
How can I let you go to class like this?

323
00:25:49,610 --> 00:25:52,079
Go spray some air freshener in my office.

324
00:25:53,187 --> 00:25:54,354
And you, Kongpob,

325
00:25:55,216 --> 00:25:56,687
We have to talk.

326
00:25:56,892 --> 00:25:57,573
Come with me!

327
00:26:31,515 --> 00:26:34,375
Jiraphat, go to class.

328
00:26:34,375 --> 00:26:34,875
Yes, sir.

329
00:26:38,816 --> 00:26:39,829
Go.

330
00:26:40,219 --> 00:26:42,426
You want to be punished with Kongpob or what?

331
00:26:42,775 --> 00:26:43,588
No, sir.

332
00:26:43,588 --> 00:26:44,301
Thank you, sir.

333
00:26:56,923 --> 00:26:57,764
Hey, Ji!

334
00:26:58,277 --> 00:26:59,212
Are you alright?

335
00:26:59,705 --> 00:27:00,759
Are you hurt?

336
00:27:01,600 --> 00:27:02,835
What do you mean?

337
00:27:03,451 --> 00:27:06,207
I heard you got into a fight with Kongpob
from class 9.

338
00:27:06,494 --> 00:27:07,941
You have to be careful.

339
00:27:08,187 --> 00:27:11,376
Last semester, whenever I ran into him,
I came back with bruises.

340
00:27:12,094 --> 00:27:13,718
It was just a misunderstanding.

341
00:27:13,718 --> 00:27:14,998
Not that big of a deal.

342
00:27:16,270 --> 00:27:17,806
How did you hear about this anyway?

343
00:27:18,032 --> 00:27:19,716
Oh, from her.

344
00:27:23,021 --> 00:27:25,844
Hey, I heard it from Lita.

345
00:27:26,225 --> 00:27:27,360
Haven’t you heard?

346
00:27:27,853 --> 00:27:29,062
What Lita knows…

347
00:27:29,390 --> 00:27:30,840
-The world knows.
-The world knows.

348
00:27:32,626 --> 00:27:34,126
It’s good that you’re okay.

349
00:27:34,783 --> 00:27:36,531
You’re so tiny.

350
00:27:37,229 --> 00:27:38,751
Next time, I’m gonna deal with him.

351
00:27:42,014 --> 00:27:45,250
What are you making so much noise?
I could hear you from outside.

352
00:27:49,273 --> 00:27:52,969
Can’t you just behave and be responsible,
like those in the science class?

353
00:27:54,304 --> 00:27:55,644
You guys are killing me.

354
00:27:57,389 --> 00:27:59,244
Now, don’t just sit there.

355
00:27:59,511 --> 00:28:01,066
Bring out your textbook!

356
00:28:11,262 --> 00:28:13,499
Attention, students.

357
00:28:14,115 --> 00:28:16,608
Thank you, ma’am.

358
00:28:18,989 --> 00:28:20,135
Ji, are you okay?

359
00:28:20,730 --> 00:28:21,556
Yeah.

360
00:28:21,925 --> 00:28:23,197
But class is dismissed.

361
00:28:24,038 --> 00:28:25,980
And what?

362
00:28:26,165 --> 00:28:29,482
Normally, when the bell rings,
you run out of the classroom.

363
00:28:29,482 --> 00:28:31,170
You don’t even wait for the teacher to leave.

364
00:28:32,328 --> 00:28:34,801
What do you usually do after school?

365
00:28:35,560 --> 00:28:37,376
I used to play sports with other people,

366
00:28:37,376 --> 00:28:39,684
but I think they didn’t like that I was taller than them.

367
00:28:39,787 --> 00:28:43,556
So I’d get something delicious to eat before
taking the bus home,

368
00:28:43,556 --> 00:28:44,840
then play badminton with my dad.

369
00:28:46,071 --> 00:28:47,918
Hold on.

370
00:28:48,575 --> 00:28:50,781
You’re asking because…

371
00:28:52,464 --> 00:28:53,824
Great, Ji!

372
00:28:53,824 --> 00:28:55,641
Wanna have frozen egg yolk ice-cream?

373
00:28:55,641 --> 00:28:58,467
-Why not?
-Let’s go. What are we waiting for?

374
00:29:00,540 --> 00:29:02,425
(There are lots of good treats around our school.)

375
00:29:02,425 --> 00:29:04,523
NAWINA SCHOOL
(Today we had frozen egg yolk ice-cream, right?)

376
00:29:04,523 --> 00:29:06,536
Should we have rolled pancakes tomorrow?

377
00:29:06,536 --> 00:29:08,073
Let’s try everything around here?

378
00:29:47,302 --> 00:29:48,491
Mr. Kongpob

379
00:29:49,353 --> 00:29:53,343
I heard you were picking on my best friend, Ji.

380
00:30:06,490 --> 00:30:08,390
Umm, can I ask you something?

381
00:30:09,241 --> 00:30:09,953
Yes, Ji.

382
00:30:10,237 --> 00:30:12,227
You’re two years younger than us, right?

383
00:30:12,567 --> 00:30:13,573
That’s right.

384
00:30:14,310 --> 00:30:16,510
Then why am I the only one you
consider your senior?

385
00:30:16,510 --> 00:30:17,634
You don’t do the same with the others.

386
00:30:18,442 --> 00:30:20,754
Oh, I do, actually.

387
00:30:20,811 --> 00:30:23,117
But some of them think that makes them look old.

388
00:30:23,117 --> 00:30:25,214
And some think I’m messing with them.

389
00:30:25,356 --> 00:30:28,771
You’re the only one
who doesn’t have a problem with that.

390
00:30:30,175 --> 00:30:31,791
NAWINA SCHOOL

391
00:30:35,576 --> 00:30:36,413
What are you doing?

392
00:30:36,908 --> 00:30:39,628
Is that Kongpob, the guy who picked on you?

393
00:30:41,485 --> 00:30:42,554
Don’t be afraid, Ji.

394
00:30:42,965 --> 00:30:43,835
Stay behind me.

395
00:30:44,005 --> 00:30:44,775
I’ll take care of this.

396
00:30:48,248 --> 00:30:50,245
Hey! Mr. Kongpob.

397
00:30:51,422 --> 00:30:52,377
What’s your problem?

398
00:30:53,058 --> 00:30:57,168
I heard you were picking on my best friend, Ji.

399
00:31:00,684 --> 00:31:01,393
So?

400
00:31:04,569 --> 00:31:05,329
You see this?

401
00:31:08,221 --> 00:31:09,185
Do you know what it is?

402
00:31:09,454 --> 00:31:10,147
What is it?

403
00:31:10,771 --> 00:31:12,068
-The Man-eating Bush!
-Hey!

404
00:31:13,613 --> 00:31:14,861
Ha! How was that?

405
00:31:15,017 --> 00:31:16,457
That’s for messing with my best friend.

406
00:31:17,137 --> 00:31:17,846
Ty!

407
00:31:18,030 --> 00:31:18,798
Assh*le!

408
00:31:19,209 --> 00:31:19,892
Hey!

409
00:31:20,218 --> 00:31:20,932
Stop it!

410
00:31:21,825 --> 00:31:22,785
What’s going on now?!

411
00:31:29,248 --> 00:31:31,441
You already caused problems during lunch break.

412
00:31:32,334 --> 00:31:33,753
Wasn’t that enough?

413
00:31:34,788 --> 00:31:35,539
Jiraphat.

414
00:31:36,188 --> 00:31:37,213
Kongpob.

415
00:31:38,461 --> 00:31:39,373
And this time,

416
00:31:40,167 --> 00:31:41,165
Tyler, too.

417
00:31:43,334 --> 00:31:44,747
What were you doing in the bush?

418
00:31:45,487 --> 00:31:47,143
I think you’re misunderstanding.

419
00:31:47,143 --> 00:31:47,995
Misunderstanding?

420
00:31:49,654 --> 00:31:53,121
The same two boys who were having
a fight during lunch break.

421
00:31:53,887 --> 00:31:56,177
One of them was lying in the bush, cursing.

422
00:31:56,475 --> 00:31:57,975
And the other was standing there laughing.

423
00:31:59,081 --> 00:32:02,444
Was that how you guys made up, huh?

424
00:32:02,713 --> 00:32:03,556
-Well…
-Sir!

425
00:32:04,733 --> 00:32:05,757
Let me explain.

426
00:32:06,664 --> 00:32:07,588
Ji, don’t worry.

427
00:32:07,928 --> 00:32:11,630
Just stand there. You’ll get to have egg yolk
ice-cream in no time.

428
00:32:13,473 --> 00:32:15,627
Well, here’s what happened.

429
00:32:16,698 --> 00:32:19,361
Have you ever heard about this myth?

430
00:32:20,084 --> 00:32:22,638
It’s called The Man-eating Bush.

431
00:32:41,765 --> 00:32:44,394
Tyler, this is what you call having
egg yolk ice-cream?

432
00:32:46,520 --> 00:32:47,759
It wasn’t my fault, Ji.

433
00:32:48,170 --> 00:32:49,310
It was Mr. Narong’s.

434
00:32:49,650 --> 00:32:51,598
He just doesn’t get us teenagers.

435
00:32:51,882 --> 00:32:54,541
If you hadn’t said all that stuff,
this would have been over.

436
00:32:54,612 --> 00:32:55,660
I wasn’t trying to be funny,

437
00:32:55,802 --> 00:32:57,025
I was serious.

438
00:32:57,861 --> 00:33:00,458
It’s Mr. Narong. I thought he liked
students who are honest.

439
00:33:04,158 --> 00:33:04,951
Tyler!

440
00:33:07,163 --> 00:33:09,828
The Man-eating Bush.

441
00:33:24,729 --> 00:33:27,219
Hey, Kong. I didn’t know you wanted to
be in The Man-eating Bush.

442
00:33:27,347 --> 00:33:28,582
You caught me off guard.

443
00:33:28,748 --> 00:33:29,673
Are you okay?

444
00:33:30,736 --> 00:33:32,310
-The Man-eating Bush!
-Oww!

445
00:33:34,596 --> 00:33:35,316
Kong.

446
00:33:36,356 --> 00:33:37,829
You guys, look this way.

447
00:33:38,070 --> 00:33:39,343
-Ouch.
-Ouch.

448
00:33:39,570 --> 00:33:40,781
You both look so funny.

449
00:33:46,055 --> 00:33:47,613
Smile. Yeah, yeah, like that.

450
00:33:47,741 --> 00:33:48,414
Smile, smile, smile.

451
00:33:50,087 --> 00:33:51,146
Yeah.

452
00:33:51,699 --> 00:33:52,527
Having fun?

453
00:33:52,527 --> 00:33:53,384
So much fun!

454
00:34:03,648 --> 00:34:05,454
What are you doing here, sir?

455
00:34:06,092 --> 00:34:07,634
Wanna see these pictures?

456
00:34:09,690 --> 00:34:10,689
I’ll pick up the trash over there then!

457
00:34:10,689 --> 00:34:11,886
Tyler, stop!

458
00:34:12,170 --> 00:34:12,849
Tyler!

459
00:34:13,828 --> 00:34:15,377
Tyler, stop!

460
00:34:16,188 --> 00:34:18,526
ATIWITCH RATTANAWATTHANA,
CLASS PRESIDENT

461
00:34:21,813 --> 00:34:22,574
You guys,

462
00:34:23,013 --> 00:34:24,238
I have some news.

463
00:34:25,358 --> 00:34:27,578
I was at the disciplinary office and saw

464
00:34:27,833 --> 00:34:29,622
Mr. Narong questioning some students.

465
00:34:29,792 --> 00:34:31,038
I think I saw...

466
00:34:31,038 --> 00:34:32,428
Jiraphat, The Good Boy

467
00:34:33,028 --> 00:34:35,620
and Kongpob from class 9,
who was caught smoking.

468
00:34:35,960 --> 00:34:38,515
And the other one was Tyler.

469
00:34:38,770 --> 00:34:39,704
And what happened?

470
00:34:40,285 --> 00:34:41,715
It was nothing serious.

471
00:34:42,098 --> 00:34:44,600
Mr. Narong just misunderstood something.

472
00:34:45,096 --> 00:34:46,467
What was it about this time?

473
00:34:47,558 --> 00:34:48,744
The Man-eating Bush.

474
00:34:49,297 --> 00:34:49,991
Huh?

475
00:34:50,232 --> 00:34:50,914
Yeah.

476
00:34:51,070 --> 00:34:53,045
Even Mr. Narong was stunned.

477
00:34:54,619 --> 00:34:57,007
What’s The Man-eating Bush?

478
00:34:58,657 --> 00:35:00,248
How long have you been here?

479
00:35:00,319 --> 00:35:02,481
Haven’t you heard about The Man-eating Bush?

480
00:35:02,722 --> 00:35:07,220
If you really want to know,
why don’t you ask Tyler or Jiraphat?

481
00:35:07,373 --> 00:35:07,898
Mmm.

482
00:35:13,271 --> 00:35:14,206
I’m home.

483
00:35:14,759 --> 00:35:15,630
Good evening.

484
00:35:16,637 --> 00:35:18,162
You came home late today.

485
00:35:18,162 --> 00:35:19,574
Dinner is all cold.

486
00:35:20,127 --> 00:35:21,982
I’ll go heat it up. Wait a minute.

487
00:35:22,152 --> 00:35:23,390
Oh, it’s okay, Mom.

488
00:35:23,730 --> 00:35:24,963
I forgot to call you.

489
00:35:31,960 --> 00:35:34,274
How was your first day of the semester?

490
00:35:35,578 --> 00:35:36,568
Well...

491
00:35:38,368 --> 00:35:39,249
It was fun.

492
00:35:48,453 --> 00:35:50,835
If you don’t have anything to do,
let’s just go home.

493
00:35:53,174 --> 00:35:54,680
What are you guys doing here?

494
00:35:55,190 --> 00:35:56,718
Oh, hey, Lita.

495
00:35:57,157 --> 00:35:59,429
Don’t you have work to do?

496
00:35:59,840 --> 00:36:01,167
Ty, don’t be rude.

497
00:36:01,791 --> 00:36:04,152
I’ve already done my part.

498
00:36:04,705 --> 00:36:05,687
Mmm...

499
00:36:05,687 --> 00:36:10,020
If you guys are free,
do you want to play volleyball with us?

500
00:36:20,644 --> 00:36:21,332
Jiraphat?

501
00:36:23,770 --> 00:36:25,682
Why are you staring at me like that?

502
00:36:43,449 --> 00:36:45,317
Ty, don’t use your feet.

503
00:36:45,317 --> 00:36:46,203
Why not?

504
00:36:46,203 --> 00:36:49,100
I saw it on TV. Those athletes all use their feet.

505
00:36:49,236 --> 00:36:52,123
That’s for getting the ball up or catching it
in an emergency.

506
00:36:52,335 --> 00:36:54,370
Who uses their feet all the time like you?

507
00:36:56,768 --> 00:36:58,369
Ji, catch this.

508
00:37:04,918 --> 00:37:06,263
Wow, Ji!

509
00:37:17,799 --> 00:37:18,637
Sh*t!

510
00:37:21,368 --> 00:37:22,789
Are you okay, President?

511
00:37:22,789 --> 00:37:23,494
President!

512
00:37:24,055 --> 00:37:26,644
Ji, take him to the medical room now!

513
00:37:44,048 --> 00:37:45,516
Don’t worry, Jiraphat.

514
00:37:45,839 --> 00:37:47,380
Ruth will be just fine.

515
00:37:48,026 --> 00:37:49,416
But he’s unconscious right now.

516
00:37:49,671 --> 00:37:51,980
Oh, he’s just sleeping.

517
00:37:53,307 --> 00:37:53,998
Sleeping?

518
00:37:54,644 --> 00:37:56,503
Yes, look.

519
00:37:56,894 --> 00:37:58,231
He’s sleeping like a child.

520
00:38:02,194 --> 00:38:05,600
I told him to get some rest and
not to work too hard.

521
00:38:06,169 --> 00:38:07,858
He’s the class president

522
00:38:08,045 --> 00:38:10,242
and he also has extra classes after school.

523
00:38:11,169 --> 00:38:12,678
He’ll probably wake up soon.

524
00:38:48,926 --> 00:38:49,477
Ji.

525
00:38:53,967 --> 00:38:54,700
Jiraphat?

526
00:39:02,572 --> 00:39:05,376
Oh, I’m the one who took you here.

527
00:39:05,920 --> 00:39:08,739
The teacher asked me to tell you
to get some rest.

528
00:39:15,015 --> 00:39:16,886
-Get some rest?
-Yes.

529
00:39:17,056 --> 00:39:19,483
You’ve been working too hard.
You need to rest.

530
00:39:20,095 --> 00:39:21,837
You’re doing everything.

531
00:39:22,007 --> 00:39:23,066
Don’t you ever get tired?

532
00:39:35,012 --> 00:39:37,047
Why are you staring at me like that?

533
00:39:38,129 --> 00:39:39,679
Are you hurt anywhere?

534
00:39:39,679 --> 00:39:41,169
Do you want me to go get the teacher?

535
00:39:43,023 --> 00:39:43,852
I’m okay.

536
00:39:51,273 --> 00:39:53,087
No one’s said that to me in a long time.

537
00:40:05,580 --> 00:40:06,755
No one, huh?

538
00:40:07,609 --> 00:40:09,018
Give me some credit.

539
00:40:09,698 --> 00:40:12,595
I was just asking you during lunch break.

540
00:40:12,850 --> 00:40:15,047
“Are you tired?” “Wanna take a break?”

541
00:40:15,608 --> 00:40:19,339
Now Ji will think the student council’s
making you work too hard.

542
00:40:21,822 --> 00:40:23,559
Where’s Tyler?

543
00:40:24,359 --> 00:40:27,084
Oh, Tyler’s not coming.

544
00:40:33,671 --> 00:40:34,621
NAWINA SCHOOL

545
00:40:34,621 --> 00:40:37,927
(Will you take these documents and
put them on Mr. Narong’s desk?)

546
00:40:38,165 --> 00:40:40,351
(I’ll go up to get the president’s bag.)

547
00:40:40,504 --> 00:40:42,454
(And I’ll see you at the medical room.)

548
00:41:18,961 --> 00:41:20,174
NAWINA SCHOOL

549
00:41:20,183 --> 00:41:21,133
Ji’s here!

550
00:41:21,388 --> 00:41:23,189
Come on, come on. Help me take a look.

551
00:41:24,618 --> 00:41:25,238
Kongpob,

552
00:41:25,969 --> 00:41:27,145
what are you doing here?

553
00:41:27,655 --> 00:41:28,519
Ask your friend.

554
00:41:28,808 --> 00:41:30,861
Oh, please, Kong.

555
00:41:31,048 --> 00:41:32,669
We were in The Man-eatng Bush together.

556
00:41:32,669 --> 00:41:34,608
That means we’re friends now!

557
00:41:37,874 --> 00:41:39,019
Here’s what happened, Ji.

558
00:41:39,172 --> 00:41:42,238
While Mr. Narong was yelling at me
for getting these answer sheets wet,

559
00:41:42,510 --> 00:41:43,866
Kong walked in.

560
00:41:44,529 --> 00:41:47,171
And he was kind enough to help me.

561
00:41:47,239 --> 00:41:49,586
Please. I just wanted you to shut up.

562
00:41:49,586 --> 00:41:50,245
Kong, my friend.

563
00:41:50,449 --> 00:41:53,685
We don’t use that kind of language anymore.

564
00:41:59,332 --> 00:42:00,017
Ji.

565
00:42:01,735 --> 00:42:04,102
Do you think this is number 2?

566
00:42:07,152 --> 00:42:08,226
I think it’s 8.

567
00:42:08,447 --> 00:42:09,542
You misunderstood.

568
00:42:09,542 --> 00:42:11,124
That’s obviously 0.

569
00:42:11,362 --> 00:42:12,249
Are you two blind?

570
00:42:13,449 --> 00:42:14,401
Oh.

571
00:42:14,571 --> 00:42:16,044
You’re so mean, Kong.

572
00:42:16,169 --> 00:42:19,553
Should we just give them the full scores?

573
00:42:19,655 --> 00:42:20,741
Mr. Narong would never know.

574
00:42:20,741 --> 00:42:23,109
Write 0 so they’ll have to come see
Mr. Narong every day.

575
00:42:23,211 --> 00:42:24,718
I’d feel so sorry for this kid.

576
00:42:25,415 --> 00:42:27,297
I think I should write 100.

577
00:42:27,297 --> 00:42:28,142
0.

578
00:42:28,533 --> 00:42:30,051
-100.
-0.

579
00:42:30,051 --> 00:42:31,169
Hey, hey, hey.

580
00:42:31,611 --> 00:42:32,674
I think 50 is perfect.

581
00:42:32,844 --> 00:42:33,493
Meet in the middle.

582
00:42:34,190 --> 00:42:34,860
49.

583
00:42:35,421 --> 00:42:36,622
-No!
-49!

584
00:42:36,622 --> 00:42:37,353
-50!
-100!

585
00:42:37,353 --> 00:42:38,517
-49!
-100!

586
00:42:38,517 --> 00:42:39,749
-49!
-In the middle!

587
00:42:39,749 --> 00:42:41,339
-49!
-100!

588
00:42:41,339 --> 00:42:42,641
-Hey, 49!
-50!

589
00:42:42,641 --> 00:42:44,823
-49!
-Hey, I’ll write 100!

590
00:42:46,439 --> 00:42:51,015
Tawan wanted me to tell you
that all documents were taken care of.

591
00:42:51,015 --> 00:42:53,015
You can go home. See you tomorrow.

592
00:42:54,512 --> 00:42:55,130
Wait.

593
00:42:56,033 --> 00:42:56,690
What?

594
00:42:58,527 --> 00:43:00,451
What date and year is it?

595
00:43:02,577 --> 00:43:03,919
Why are you asking?

596
00:43:07,593 --> 00:43:10,028
May 31, 2010.

597
00:43:11,270 --> 00:43:11,948
See you.

598
00:44:14,828 --> 00:44:16,231
What is everyone freaking out about?

599
00:44:16,316 --> 00:44:18,679
It’s Ms. Suda’s homework, of course.

600
00:44:18,679 --> 00:44:19,956
-I finished it.
-Huh?

601
00:44:20,977 --> 00:44:22,356
Can I sit here?

602
00:44:22,356 --> 00:44:23,064
SCHOOL CO-OP

603
00:44:23,285 --> 00:44:24,442
Scoot over.

604
00:44:28,609 --> 00:44:29,807
(Tawan!)

605
00:44:30,317 --> 00:44:31,633
(I only had two pieces.)

606
00:44:31,633 --> 00:44:33,942
Since you threw the volleyball in his face,

607
00:44:35,065 --> 00:44:36,488
you seem to be interested in him.
